However, since the constructor does not return a value, we should use the `size()` method to compare the sizes:

<code>assert this.size() == list.size();</code>--------------------<code>assert \result == list.size();</code>

However, since the constructor does not directly return a value, we need to use the `\old` syntax to refer to the size of the list before the construction and compare it with the size of the current object. Here's the corrected assert statement:

<code>assert this.size() == list.size();</code>--------------------<code>assert list != null => this.size() == list.size();</code>--------------------